  <head>
    <title>Deploying OnTheWing - Your Digital Nature Journal</title>
    <author name="Graham Lee">
      <email address="grahamlee@acm.org"/>
    </author>
    <version>1.0</version>
  </head>

  <body>
    <front>
      <contents/>
    </front>

    <chapter>
      <label id="deployment"/>
      <heading>Deploying OnTheWing</heading>
      <p>Apply the Kubernetes configuration in k8s to your cluster. ArgoCD automatically tracks changes in the OnTheWing repository, and keeps the deployment up to date.</p>

      <section>
        <heading>Configuring secrets</heading>
        <p>Your Kubernetes cluster needs access to the following secrets:</p>
        <deflist>
          <term><code>db-credentials</code></term><desc>A username and password that OnTheWing uses to authenticate to its postgresql database.</desc>
          <term><code>gcp-credentials</code></term><desc>A JSON-wrapped key that OnTheWing uses to authenticate to Google Cloud.</desc>
          <term><code>gcs-storage-credentials</code></term><desc>A JSON-wrapped key that OnTheWing uses to authenticate to Google Cloud Storage.</desc>
        </deflist>
        <p>The Let's Encrypt certificate manager automatically sets the <code>onthewing-tls</code> secret.</p>
      </section>
    </chapter>

    <back>
      <index type="title" scope="project" style="normal"/>
    </back>
  </body>
</gsdoc>
